 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 11:11:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 091/106] ASoC: qdsp6: q6asm: knob for the stream
 post-processing topology

The vendor opens its in-call streams with a post-processing topology of
its own out of ACDB (0x10000018 on the reference device) where we always
ask for none, and it was the last field of the whole command stream that
still differed.

It cannot be used here: the DSP answers ADSP_EUNSUPPORTED to it, which
makes sense - that topology lives in the vendor's ACDB and we never load
one. Default stays at none.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
index 8fd2af585..1409b5f88 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
@@ -114,6 +114,11 @@ struct asm_multi_channel_pcm_fmt_blk_v2 {
  * format block the DSP is given (48 bytes against 20), so a DSP that only
  * expects v5 on a path would be reading our block wrong.
  */
+static uint popp_topology;
+module_param(popp_topology, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(popp_topology,
+		 "stream post-processing topology (0 = none, as mainline always did)");
+
 static bool pcm_fmt_v5 = true;
 module_param(pcm_fmt_v5, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(pcm_fmt_v5, "open PCM streams with media format v5 (vendor) instead of v2");
@@ -977,7 +982,14 @@ int q6asm_open_write(struct audio_client *ac, uint32_t stream_id,
 	/* source endpoint : matrix */
 	open->sink_endpointype = ASM_END_POINT_DEVICE_MATRIX;
 	open->bits_per_sample = bits_per_sample;
-	open->postprocopo_id = ASM_NULL_POPP_TOPOLOGY;
+	/*
+	 * The vendor opens its in-call streams with a post-processing topology
+	 * of its own (0x10000018 on the reference device), out of ACDB, where
+	 * we have always asked for none. It is the last field of the whole
+	 * command stream that still differs, so it is a parameter to try.
+	 */
+	open->postprocopo_id = popp_topology ? popp_topology
+					     : ASM_NULL_POPP_TOPOLOGY;
 
 	switch (format) {
 	case SND_AUDIOCODEC_MP3:
